Subject: [PATCH 47/50] [ir] resolve conditional Phi inputs when tracking
 bindless texture handles (#4551)

- [x] I have read and followed the [Contribution Guidelines](https://git.eden-emu.dev/eden-emu/eden/src/branch/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-contributions).
- [x] I have read and followed the [AI Policy](https://git.eden-emu.dev/eden-emu/eden/src/branch/master/docs/policies/AI.md).
- [x] I have read and followed the [Coding Guidelines](https://git.eden-emu.dev/eden-emu/eden/src/branch/master/docs/policies/Coding.md) to the best of my ability.

-------------------
Aimed to fix Ender Magnolia missing shader textures. Main example is Yolvan character bullets.

By using windows version of the game, dxvk lib to make it vulkan, and renderdoc, it was possible to capture bullets, and by tracking backward composition and comparing with a similar scene from eden with missing bullets, it was possible to unveil the missing functionality: conditional Phi inputs resolve for bindless handles.
By ignoring the boolean predicate register in the shader, handles for these shaders were resolving to some old value instead of proper live conditional ones.

TESTS:
-Compare Yolvan bullets
-Usual roam on main titles for regression check.

